<!-- What a NativeAOT or trimmed app must keep for data binding, because binding finds members by name at run time and nothing in the
     program refers to them. Every line is needed: the smoke test fails without it (see "Binding and trimming" in docs/backends.md).

     The control side used to need a Majorsilence.Forms/Control entry here too (the property that is bound, and the event the
     control raises when it changes; without the event a bound control still shows the view model, but edits never reach it).
     Majorsilence.Forms now ships that root itself, embedded in the assembly (#290, src/Majorsilence.Forms/ILLink.Descriptors.xml);
     this file no longer declares it, and the smoke test passing is what proves the embedded one is doing its job. -->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="Majorsilence.Forms.AotSmoke">
    <!-- The view-model side: every property a binding names. A missing one used to not be an error, the binding would just never
         move a value for a reflective lookup the trimmer could not see either; fixed in #290 for the "wrong name" case
         (DataBindings.Add now throws), but a property trimmed out of the assembly for being otherwise unreferenced looks the same
         as a wrong name from the binding's point of view, so it still has to be rooted here. -->
    <type fullname="SmokeViewModel">
      <property name="Title" />
      <property name="Name" />
    </type>
  </assembly>
</linker>
